menu "ESP RainMaker Work Queue (defaults)"

    config ESP_RMAKER_WORK_QUEUE_SIZE
        int "ESP RainMaker Work Queue size"
        range 1 256
        default 8
        help
            Maximum number of pending jobs in the ESP RainMaker Work Queue.
            Each entry uses 8 bytes of internal RAM.

    config ESP_RMAKER_WORK_QUEUE_TASK_STACK
        int "ESP RainMaker Work Queue Task stack"
        default 5120
        help
            Stack size in bytes for the ESP RainMaker Work Queue Task.

    config ESP_RMAKER_WORK_QUEUE_TASK_PRIORITY
        int "ESP RainMaker Work Queue Task priority"
        default 5
        help
            Priority for the ESP RainMaker Work Queue Task. Not recommended to be changed
            unless you really need it.

    config ESP_RMAKER_WORK_QUEUE_PREFER_EXT_RAM
        bool "Prefer external RAM for the ESP RainMaker Work Queue Task stack"
        depends on SPIRAM_ALLOW_STACK_EXTERNAL_MEMORY || FREERTOS_TASK_CREATE_ALLOW_EXT_MEM
        default n
        help
            Whether to prefer to allocate the ESP RainMaker Work Queue Task
            stack in external RAM (SPIRAM), with internal-RAM fallback. The
            TCB is always kept in internal RAM.

            WARNING: A task with its stack in SPIRAM will fault if code runs
            while the flash cache is disabled (e.g. during any NVS/flash
            write, since SPIRAM shares the cache). Do NOT enable this unless
            you can guarantee that no work function scheduled on this queue
            performs flash/NVS writes (or any other cache-disabling
            operation). The global RainMaker work queue does perform NVS
            writes, so leaving this at 'n' is strongly recommended.

endmenu
